{"name":"Rumours","hex":"#744245","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rumours","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of rumour"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of rumour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rumours"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rumours (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumours is the eleventh studio album by the British and American rock band Fleetwood Mac, released on 4 February 1977, by Warner Bros. Records. Largely recorded in California in 1976, it was produced by the band with Ken Caillat and Richard Dashut. The recording sessions took place as the band members dealt with breakups with one another and struggled with heavy drug use, both of which shaped the album's direction and lyrics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/FMacRumours.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumours_(album)","wikidata":"Q695405"},{"title":"Rumours (2024 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumours is a 2024 comedy horror film written and directed by Guy Maddin, Evan Johnson, and Galen Johnson. The film stars Cate Blanchett, Charles Dance, Roy Dupuis, Denis Ménochet, Nikki Amuka-Bird, Rolando Ravello, Takehiro Hira, Zlatko Burić, and Alicia Vikander."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/Rumours_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumours_(2024_film)","wikidata":"Q124256183"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fb/FMacRumours.PNG/250px-FMacRumours.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/FMacRumours.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fb/FMacRumours.PNG/25